module gunbc.plans.planning_consolidation

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, MarkdownListItem }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, p, li, ul, ol, quote }

fn planning_consolidation_row(id: String, location: String, answers: String, io: String, finding: String) -> MarkdownListItem {
  li(text: concat(concat(concat(concat(concat(concat(concat(concat("**", id), ".** "), location), " **Answers:** "), answers), concat(" **In/out:** ", io)), " **Finding:** "), finding))
}

fn planning_consolidation_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    quote(blocks: [
      p(text: "**Goal:** decide, from first principles, which planning concerns exist and give each exactly one home, so that a plan, a unit of work, its state, its decisions and its debt cannot be stated twice or drift apart. `gunbc.design_argument::planning_has_one_home` says a plan has one home; this plan finds out what \"a plan\" decomposes into before that claim is applied further."),
      p(text: "**Operator direction (2026-11-10, session bright-ibex-807):** the plans and the roadmap must be consolidated, from first principles; first write up the inventory and a proposed decomposition for the operator to rule on. Nothing in sections 3 or 4 is decided until the operator rules (section 5)."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "1. Why this was missed"),
    p(text: "The 2026-11-08 planning rework (T1 to T14) consolidated planning FACTS and READS: plan data off the build path (T1, T2), the side task store deleted (T5), one home for acceptance (T6), dead plans and nodes deleted (T7, T8), private rows naming public ids (T13), ledgers out of code imports (T14). Every item started from a symptom: a 90-minute plan-only merge, or one fact with several homes. None asked whether `gunbc.plans` and `gunbc.roadmap` are two concepts or one; both were treated as given carriers. The step that would have put them side by side (T3/T4, one `plan/` tree) was replaced by the closure approach because it moved about 600 files, and the question went with it."),
    h2(text: "2. Inventory (measured at origin/main 2026-11-10)"),
    p(text: "Each row: where it lives, the question it answers, what goes in and out, and what the reading found. Counts are from `git grep` / `git show` at the named revision; a negative search is evidence of absence by name only."),
    ul(items: [
      planning_consolidation_row(id: "C1", location: "`gunbc.plans.*`, 15 files; 13 registered in `gunbc.plan_registry` `all_plans`.", answers: "what we intend to do and why: goal, displaced cost, inventory, phases, decisions, done-when.", io: "In: authored prose. Out: `plan_documentation_wet` renders markdown on demand; `gunbc.doc_graph_roots` and the plan lens read `all_plans`.", finding: "`gunbc.plan` `Plan` is `{ slug, title, body: List<MarkdownBlock>, retirement, projection }`: phases, decisions and done-when are markdown PROSE, so nothing can reference a phase, check its dependencies, or derive its state. `md_helpers` is a markdown helper, not a plan (imported by `gunbc.design_document`). `demand_restatement_follow_up` is a plan file that is not in `all_plans`."),
      planning_consolidation_row(id: "C2", location: "`gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_authority` (6,595 lines, 272 node rows, 155 edge rows) over `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model` `RoadmapNode`.", answers: "what the units of work are, how they depend on each other, who may take them and how they are dispatched.", io: "In: authored rows. Out: the daily workspace page, the belt (dispatch), forecasts, the runtime plan.", finding: "`RoadmapNode` is typed (minted identity, edges, dispatch, execution contract, sizing) and `roadmap_model` records the operator ruling of 2026-09-30 that a project, a milestone and a task are ONE record. Rows still carry long `boundary` and `approach` prose that restates plan content."),
      planning_consolidation_row(id: "C3", location: "Plan to roadmap links: `RoadmapNode.carriers: List<Pointer>` with `Pointer { label, path: String }`; plus plan names inside row prose.", answers: "which plan a node executes.", io: "In: a file path or a string. Out: `pointer_resolves` checks only that the path names an existing document.", finding: "Two typed carriers in all of roadmap_authority. Fourteen plan citations are free text, and three name plans the 2026-11-08 reset deleted (`gunbc.plans.convergence_coverage_program`, `gunbc.plans.durable_work_handoff`, `gunbc.plans.ensure_closure_design`), which nothing reports. No plan names a roadmap node, and neither tree imports the other."),
      planning_consolidation_row(id: "C4", location: "The roadmap event log (`gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_event_log`, origin's `roadmap-events` branch).", answers: "what has happened to a node.", io: "In: `issue_command_apply` appends. Out: node standings for the page, belt and acceptance.", finding: "Kinds: claimed, progress, blocked, handed_back, released, result_returned, published, verification_failed, receipt, retired and the comment kinds; acceptance arrives with T6 (#16189). This is already one home for state."),
      planning_consolidation_row(id: "C5", location: "`gunbc.design_ruling` (dated operator rulings).", answers: "what was decided, when, on whose words.", io: "In: authored rows. Out: cited from DESIGN.md and plans by symbol.", finding: "Plans also record operator decisions inline in their prose (for example read_set_convergence's P2 and P4 amendments), so a decision can live in two places."),
      planning_consolidation_row(id: "C6", location: "Debt with a trigger: `gunbc.rung_drop`, `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode`, `gunbc.integration_concern` (2,241 lines; imported only by its witness), plan retirement conditions, dissolution conditions on scaffolds.", answers: "what is owed, and what ends it.", io: "Authored rows; `gunbc.design_ledgers` renders combined views.", finding: "Several ledger shapes for one concept, an obligation with a discharge trigger; whether they are one concept is section 3's question, not decided here."),
      planning_consolidation_row(id: "C7", location: "Outside this repository: dashboard work items (`dashboard-ops work-items`, the control plane's store); the private repository's plan rows; the control plane's planning directories (being deleted, child adhoc-455df2cb-513).", answers: "who is doing what now; private or cross-repository intent.", io: "Work items carry a free-text brief; private rows name public node ids (gunbc-private#290).", finding: "Nothing requires a work item to name the roadmap node or plan phase it executes, so the dashboard can become a second planning home."),
      planning_consolidation_row(id: "C8", location: "Projections: plan markdown (`gunbc.plan_documentation`), the daily workspace page (`gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_page`), DESIGN.md's ledger views.", answers: "how a person reads the above.", io: "Rendered from C1, C2, C4.", finding: "Projections, not homes; the daily workspace returns 503 until T6 deploys (gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence P6)."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "3. Proposed decomposition (for the operator to rule on)"),
    p(text: "The atomic concerns, each a question with one authority, by the test in `gunbc.design_argument::atomic_concern`:"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**Intent:** the result wanted, the outcomes that are unacceptable, the displaced cost. Proposed home: the node that owns the work (a project node), as typed fields, not a separate prose document."),
      li(text: "**Decomposition:** which units of work exist and their dependency order. Proposed home: roadmap nodes and edges ONLY. A plan's phase list is the same fact as its child nodes and their edges, so keeping both is a fork."),
      li(text: "**Done-when:** what must hold by execution. Proposed home: the node's acceptance criteria, consumed by the acceptance receipt (C4)."),
      li(text: "**State:** claimed, blocked, retired, accepted. Home: the event log (C4); already true, T6 completes it."),
      li(text: "**Decision:** a dated operator ruling. Home: `gunbc.design_ruling`; a plan or node cites it by symbol and never restates it."),
      li(text: "**Assignment:** which session is executing which node. Home: the dashboard work item, which must name the node it executes (the control plane enforces it)."),
      li(text: "**Debt:** an obligation with its discharge trigger. Home: undecided; C6 lists the candidates."),
      li(text: "**Reasoning:** the prose a person needs to understand a choice (inventory, measurements, why). Stays prose, attached to the node it explains, cited by symbol."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Operator ruling on D1 (2026-11-10, session bright-ibex-807):** plans become DESIGNS; a design carries a WORK-ITEM SECTION built from the same construct the daily workspace shows; the ROADMAP consumes designs' work items and schedules them into concrete time periods. So the homes are: a design owns intent, reasoning, decision citations and its own decomposition into work items (with their dependencies and done-when); the roadmap owns only WHEN, the assignment of work items to time periods; the event log owns state; the dashboard work item owns who is executing. The dependency runs one way: the roadmap imports designs, designs never import the roadmap. This replaces the section-3 proposal that plans dissolve into roadmap nodes; the 2026-09-30 one-record ruling still holds, but the record now lives in the design that owns the work, not in a roadmap file."),
    h2(text: "4. Phases (Q0 now; Q1 onward after D4 to D6)"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**Q0, now and independent of the ruling:** the three dangling plan citations in roadmap prose (C3) and `demand_restatement_follow_up`'s missing registration are defects under any decomposition; fix or delete them. Move `md_helpers` out of the plans tree."),
      li(text: "**Q1, the work-item construct:** move the one-record type (today `gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_model` `RoadmapNode`: minted identity, dispatch, execution contract, done-when, dependencies) to a home the design and the roadmap both import, so a design's work-item section and the daily workspace render the same record. Typed references replace `Pointer { path: String }`, so a renamed or deleted target fails loudly."),
      li(text: "**Q2, designs:** `gunbc.plans` becomes `gunbc.designs` and `gunbc.plan` `Plan` becomes a `Design` with typed sections (intent, reasoning, decision citations, work items) in place of one markdown body; one live plan migrates end to end as the specimen (proposed: `gunbc.plans.read_set_convergence`, whose phases are already discrete), cut over at the root (`gunbc.design_argument::replacement_migration`)."),
      li(text: "**Q3, the roadmap schedules:** the roadmap's node rows move into the work-item sections of the designs that own them (a row with no owning design gets one, or is deleted as unread); the roadmap keeps only the schedule: which work items fall in which time period, in what order. The page, belt and dispatch read work items through it."),
      li(text: "**Q4:** the remaining plans migrate; restated `boundary` and `approach` prose is trimmed to references; DESIGN.md's planning claim is updated to name designs and the roadmap's scheduling role. (Requiring every dashboard work item to name the design work item it executes is deferred by D3.)"),
      li(text: "**Q5, debt (D2):** inventory each debt ledger's row shape, trigger form and consumers, decide the one obligation-with-trigger record and its home, and migrate the ledgers to it, deleting each old ledger as it empties."),
    ]),
    h2(text: "5. Decisions for the operator"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "**D1, relation: RULED 2026-11-10** (above): plans become designs with a work-item section; the roadmap consumes them and schedules them in time periods."),
      li(text: "**D2, debt: RULED 2026-11-10:** the debt ledgers (rung drops, recurring failure modes, integration concerns, dissolution conditions) are to be consolidated soon, as one concept: an obligation with its discharge trigger (Q5). Open within it: whether a design's open debt sits in its work-item section."),
      li(text: "**D3, assignment: RULED 2026-11-10, not yet:** the control plane does not require a dashboard work item to name a design work item for now; Q4's control-plane clause is deferred, and the dashboard can still drift into a second planning home until it is taken up."),
      li(text: "**D4, specimen:** which plan migrates first (Q2)."),
      li(text: "**D5, the time period:** the roadmap's unit of time (a week, a month, a named cycle), and whether a scheduled period is a commitment or a forecast (the roadmap's existing forecasts compute dates today)."),
      li(text: "**D6, the name:** `design` already names DESIGN.md, `gunbc.design_argument`, `gunbc.design_document` and `gunbc.design_ruling`, which are the project's design argument, not a piece of work. A work design and THE design argument sharing one word is the meaning-fork `gunbc.design_argument::single_authority` warns about unless the module paths keep them apart; confirm `gunbc.designs.*` (plural, a distinct namespace) or choose another word."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data planning_consolidation_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "planning-consolidation",
  title: "Planning consolidation: one home per planning concern",
  body: planning_consolidation_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "The operator has ruled D1 to D6 and every phase the ruling admits has landed: each planning concern in section 3 has one home, no plan or roadmap row restates another's fact, and this plan has itself been migrated into the ruled home or deleted.") },
}
